[{"id":"VRCE-2-91-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":91,"verse":1,"english":"Pacifying Sumitrā's son, Laksmana, transported with rage and eager for encounter, Rama addressed him, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.789,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-97-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2091001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ed02d6266a7bcaf58e0a82aa08c646e2a8e15ac8985e3b9949c3fd1f716df36e","compact":"fd165b5b68e72a4c3ba3d3c3bf33ea49691dc2716c7624935f4a39eae5b6c5a8","nasal":"d4ec72289929ab91e67ccb9c6966ebf7d455c96d72aea2ca59ee38a961574712"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-91-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":91,"verse":2,"english":"When the mighty Bharata possessed of high spirits has himself come here, what is the use of the bow or the sword or the shield?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.571,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-97-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2091002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e80e87c1cef559d1fbd43d872f5f7156351e7d33012b335abf7ab5b865d3e3b8","compact":"8d1b6d0ab68739ff36e2a744db26ee7e144c38e438102f3e7ff04ecaf5e68b56","nasal":"8d1b6d0ab68739ff36e2a744db26ee7e144c38e438102f3e7ff04ecaf5e68b56"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-91-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":91,"verse":3,"english":"And the season being fit. meet it is that Bharata should see us. He does not even in thought act against us.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.701,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-97-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2091003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0938e9cbbf89afa0a4ea9303038613a78f7d225c2a00a7da7639d7769c5d314b","compact":"de3d1cbee1b266dc2c1cffcfa4e7c7b3b3e7098bc3f2a8138b807d3629e10c9a","nasal":"de3d1cbee1b266dc2c1cffcfa4e7c7b3b3e7098bc3f2a8138b807d3629e10c9a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-91-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":91,"verse":4,"english":"Has ere this Bharata done you any bad turn? Or did he tell you any thing so alarming that today you stand in fear of him?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.691,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-97-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2091004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a92d097e71a84c1c9525e7440b243f3c6e3356fca176ce880c757a4d5fcc961a","compact":"3b7e153a21ea2c7e666fdcf9475e046b87096cde7e278fec052b282ff0726085","nasal":"ee52b05d955db96e13b5e0014096e898ccf481cc60fc0fb9426f247a1575f18c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-91-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":91,"verse":5,"english":"Certainly you ought not to say cruel or unpleasant words in relation to Bharata, if wrong be done to Bharata, I shall consider myself as wornged.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-97-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2091005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"74538d232e5177ff1be6e279a421a3612d014d3f08f50962d4336a17863902ab","compact":"56ff4578d102323e53200086bef293d51871e23f1ce172d627d1a76319ca15e4","nasal":"56ff4578d102323e53200086bef293d51871e23f1ce172d627d1a76319ca15e4"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-91-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":91,"verse":6,"english":"Do sons, in times of peril, ever slay their father, or brothers their brother like to their life, O son of Sumitrā?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-97-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2091006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fbb4642a0ea40ef0ff4b01d5477118910711f88ac1941f113042094df57e3611","compact":"f8337e4d2a77340f1b96dd55045bf2e9cb5546e3ef270bd28d8af1081863c89b","nasal":"f8337e4d2a77340f1b96dd55045bf2e9cb5546e3ef270bd28d8af1081863c89b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-91-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":91,"verse":7,"english":"If you speak thus for the sake of the monarchy, on seeing Bharata, I will say to him, \"Make over the kingdom to this one/\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-97-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2091007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6e7d727f2ff3d58e066cdceea7cbb9c78d7ed078d311a69b467f4bcd49473be7","compact":"1516bad77b70d664662c9dc51c28ac7ddcdc6b6379982dd67f7304349896bddd","nasal":"1516bad77b70d664662c9dc51c28ac7ddcdc6b6379982dd67f7304349896bddd"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-91-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":91,"verse":8,"english":"Earnestly exhorted by me, saying, “Do you place the kingdom in his hands', he will say, \"Very well'.\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-97-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2091008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ca2e2ba7e79b6d94752c846a663508a6bea1d430388d70ab1c3e3d244e9bb8c0","compact":"a8e78ee0f5052e9dad877a08258ee24563a0332b93b4ceaa5d9ef352950eb7b1","nasal":"a8e78ee0f5052e9dad877a08258ee24563a0332b93b4ceaa5d9ef352950eb7b1"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-91-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":91,"verse":9,"english":"Thus addressed by his brother of a virtuous disposition, Laksmana ever engaged in Rama's good, from shame seemed to enter into his body.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-97-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2091009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6d